==Strategy==
Compared to [[Pufferfish Pulsar (Merciless)|Pufferfish Pulsar]]'s cash drought, this stage opts to supply you with multiple free sources of money in Mistress Celeboodle and Gabriels, in exchange for adding two more Puffsleys as well as support from Zir Zeal and Chickful A. There aren't many Chickful A or Zir Zeal waves, so assuming you are able to deal with them in a timely matter there will not be much pushing power to speak of. The main problem with this stage, however, will be the threat of the three Puffsleys, which will obliterate all of your units thanks to their high damage and Omni Strike if unsynced. To counter this, your main goal for this stage will be syncing up all three Puffsleys by using [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]'s [[Wave Attack|Wave]] to knock them all back, then using [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] on one of the peons to bait hits from all three. This will result in all of them entering their backswing at the same time, meaning the next time they are all hit with another Wave, they will all attack the same target, greatly simplifying the stage.

==='''Key Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: A Talented Bahamut has extremely high damage as well as Explosions, which will cause the Puffsleys to rebound multiple times and take tons of damage. While it is best to use Bahamut against the three Puffsleys near the end of the stage to kill them faster alongside a meatshield, you can also use your first Bahamut for when the two other Puffsleys first spawn to get some quick damage off.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]: Cadaver is the quickest way to kill the Zir Zeal and get him out of the stage. While BearCat does not actually outrange him, speed-clipping means BearCat is able to hit Zeal occasionally so long as Zeal is attacking a meatshield in front of him. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] is another alternative to Cadaver, being able to actually outrange Zeal, but is much less spammable which hurts its viability a bit in Research-based lineups.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Its level 7 Waves are key to syncing up all three Puffsleys alongside Boulder, and Jelly Dumpling is naturally able to connect against almost every enemy in the stage. Note that Jelly Dumpling's interaction with Gabriel is always a loss due to Gabriel's very high speed and short foreswing, so you must block him with a meatshield first.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Alongside Jelly Dumpling, Boulder is integral to syncing up all of the Puffsleys. Boulder is also good here to bait Zeal and Chickful A hits, as well as tank Celeboodle hits. Note that when sending Boulder to sync the Puffsleys, you must not use Boulder to damage a Puffsley directly, since its damage can cause a Puffsley to flinch and desync him from the rest.
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]: Needed to help Bahamut chain attacks, as well as just being a good meatshield for Zeal.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train moves fast and has good damage, being able to snipe a peon or hit Chickful A for a decent amount. Like Boulder, be sure not to use Bullet Train against a Puffsley once they're synced up.

==='''Useful Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can moves fast and deals good damage, being able to get extra money from the Mistress Celeboodles to ensure you'll never run out of cash or damage Chickful A to get it out of the battle quicker. However, Can Can is not super good once the other two Puffsleys spawn due to Can Can being able to desync a Puffsley by hitting it.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: Doron is a big version of Jelly Dumpling, having a good Omni and a [[Surge Attack]]. Note that it is much harder to sync up the Puffsleys using Doron instead of Jelly Dumpling due to the inaccuracy of the Surge.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]] nukers are valuable here to reduce the amount of times you have to deal with rebounding Puffsleys. Examples include [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]], and [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]].
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Balrog is effectively an Uber Can Can, so he'll perform about as well. Balrog's crazy high damage and spammability means that he can quickly delete the supporting peons as well as get huge damage off the first Puffsley while it's isolated.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Although Cosmo's speed-clipping issue can often get him killed, his enormous damage and range more than make up for it. He can kill the Puffsley's Comets in just a few hits and Freeze Chickful A.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo is extremely spammable and has Massive Damage vs. Angels, meaning that he can quickly turn Chickful A into Chick-fil-A.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]]: They perform about as well as [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]], having huge range and damage. As a bonus, they also have a short Slow and Mini-Surges to cause the Puffsleys to rebound twice.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: With his insane damage against Traited and good health, Izanagi can nuke down all three Puffsley's Comets and Chickful As.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Nighthunter Saki]]: In Evolved Form, she is capable of outranging Puffsley's Comet and nuking away both them and Zir Zeal. Her quick cooldown also means that she can be quickly redeployed if she dies.

