'''Battle''': The main thing you want to do before the other two Puffsleys appear is for you to cripple the first Chickful A and kill the first two Zir Zeals. To that end, constantly spam Manic Eraser and Li'l Mohawk while Jelly Dumpling and Bullet Train deal good damage to the first Puffsley. While Zeal may seem annoying with this lineup, a bunch of meatshields alongside Boulder should ensure he doesn't push much. Jelly Dumpling alongside Bullet Train will drain Zeal's health, and your spam of Cadavers will Z-Kill him. Even if Cadaver doesn't get the kill, it's not too hard to deal with him after he revives. When the next two Puffsleys appear, try to prevent them from not taking too much ground with your meatshield spam, then do the Jelly Dumpling into Boulder trick mentioned previously to sync them all up. Chickful A should still be alive at this point, so you should always have an enemy to use your Boulder into. From here, you need to ensure that the only damage the Puffsleys take are from Jelly Dumpling Waves, since anything else will desync at least one of them. The next Zeal that appears may seem like a bit of a hassle to deal with, but as long as you have been sending meatshields out to prevent the next Puffsley hit from wiping your base out you should have a good amount of time and stage length to deal with the Zeal. Once it dies, Puffsley may roll to your base, which is where the Iron Wall Cannon comes in to stall the Puffsleys for a moment. At this point, there are now no more Zeals left, so you can begin cleaning up the Chickful As using Bullet Train and Jelly Dumpling. Once all the Chickful As are dead, clean up and win.

